WEBVTT

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:11.760
This is Izakaya Nobu.

00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:16.490
It's an ordinary izakaya, but 
there is one extraordinary thing.

00:00:13.060 --> 00:00:14.990
<b>Nobuyuki Yazawa (32)
 Owner of the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.600
Our front door opens into 
a parallel universe!

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.000
<b>Shinobu Senke (23)
 Waitress at the izakaya "Nobu"</b>

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Isekai Izakaya

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.010
Japanese Food From Another World

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:33.010
<b>The Company Commander's Weakness</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:35.680
<b>Izakaya Nobu</b>

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:36.840
<b>Sake</b>

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:38.390
That is to say, squid.

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.990
<b>Grilled Squid Tentacles</b>

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:41.990
<b>An irresistible treat, try it with 
shichimi chili powder mayonnaise.</b>

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:40.400
Squid?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:41.980
Right. Squid.

00:00:41.980 --> 00:00:44.280
By squid, do you mean actual squid?

00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.280
<b>Eva (14)
Dishwasher at Nobu.
Resident of Ancient City Aitheria</b>

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.160
<b>Berthold (32)
 Company commander of the Aitheria 
palace guard, known as the "Devil"</b>

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.150
That's right, it's squidiculous!

00:00:47.150 --> 00:00:51.790
It's weird to know there's
 something you don't like.

00:00:51.790 --> 00:00:53.970
I can't handle squid.

00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:55.160
Squid is the one thing I won't eat.

00:00:55.170 --> 00:00:59.540
So why do you absolutely have to eat it?

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:02.880
Because they'll be serving it 
at the marriage interview.

00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:04.040
Marriage interview?

00:01:04.040 --> 00:01:06.050
Berthold-san, you?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:08.630
She's the daughter of one of my relatives.

00:01:08.630 --> 00:01:09.870
Her name is Hermina.

00:01:09.870 --> 00:01:12.480
She has a nice disposition, and she's cute.

00:01:13.230 --> 00:01:15.000
So that's what it is.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.920
You understand how it is, Shinobu-chan.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:21.660
If all goes well, I plan to invite 
her to live with me here.

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:25.830
I'll be bringing her here, too, 
so I'm counting on you for that.

00:01:25.830 --> 00:01:29.060
But, why are they serving squid?

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:32.660
Because my potential father-in-law is 
a fisherman specializing in squid.

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:36.570
Ah, then they'll serve it for sure.

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.720
They most definitely will.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.720
But that isn't just a problem for that 
one day, it's a lifelong hurdle.

00:01:42.720 --> 00:01:45.640
You'll be swimming in good squid, then...

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:47.340
I'm jealous.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:51.370
You'd like to be in my place, 
but that's the problem.

00:01:51.370 --> 00:01:55.590
If I don't conquer this squid 
here and now, I'm done for.

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:59.730
<b>Edwin (70) 
Deacon of the ancient city Aitheria</b>

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.970
Who would've thought that the company 
commander they call the "Devil" is scared of squid?

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.360
Let's help him out, Taishou!

00:02:03.630 --> 00:02:04.380
Yes.

00:02:04.720 --> 00:02:07.370
I'll make you various dishes 
so you can try them all.

00:02:07.370 --> 00:02:10.370
Uh, thank you, Taishou.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.380
<b>Ika Soumen</b>

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:13.380
<b>A fusion of supple texture and
 freshness. Let's slurp them up.</b>

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:13.380
<b>Sparkle Sparkle</b>

00:02:10.770 --> 00:02:12.790
We start with ika soumen.

00:02:11.210 --> 00:02:13.380
<b>Sparkle Sparkle</b>

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:17.120
<b>Shine Shine</b>

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.820
Ika... soumen?

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.170
You eat it together with the broth.

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:21.100
I didn't know this was the color of squid.

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:22.730
The degree of freshness is different.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:23.680
Degree of freshness?

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:27.040
Fresh squid is almost translucent.

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.190
It was still recently alive, so the 
degree of sweetness is something else.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.680
I see.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.180
It's delicious!

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:35.880
Just think of it as noodles 
and eat it right up!

00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:36.750
Right up?

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:37.650
Right up.

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.100
Good luck, Berthold-san.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.910
<b>Sparkle Sparkle</b>

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:49.730
<i>Go.</i>

00:02:49.780 --> 00:02:50.760
<i>Go!</i>

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:51.990
I can't!

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:53.970
<i>He squidn't go.</i>

00:02:54.310 --> 00:02:56.940
I don't think I should start with it raw.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.490
Father, what's that?

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.760
<b>Droop</b>

00:02:59.810 --> 00:03:01.760
It's squid shiokara.

00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:12.000
Ah, there's no combination more 
sinful than shiokara and reishu.

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.280
<b>Shiokara</b>

00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:18.280
<b>The salty, pungent taste 
gets you hooked.</b>

00:03:12.230 --> 00:03:16.550
Shiokara is bits of squid flesh 
and organs, pickled in salt.

00:03:16.550 --> 00:03:20.270
It's not just good with sake, 
it's also excellent with rice.

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.660
D-Did you say organs?!

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:25.390
Why don't you try some?

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.020
Here.

00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.520
Come on, go.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:37.050
<i>Go.</i>

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.030
<i>Go!</i>

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:40.290
No, I'll pass!

00:03:40.290 --> 00:03:42.290
<i>He squidn't go.</i>

00:03:42.560 --> 00:03:45.810
You don't have to force 
yourself, Berthold-san.

00:03:45.810 --> 00:03:47.540
Taishou, what's next?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:49.930
How about squid braised in ginger?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.550
<b>Ginger-braised Squid</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.550
<b>The ginger aroma will 
awaken your appetite</b>

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.860
Taishou's ginger-braised squid 
has no fishy smell to it at all.

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:56.950
<b>Steam Steam</b>

00:03:54.860 --> 00:03:58.540
<i>Even then, it's still squid...</i>

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:00.070
He doesn't like this, either.

00:04:00.070 --> 00:04:01.250
Well, then...

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.890
<b>Squid Balls</b>

00:04:02.550 --> 00:04:05.890
<b>A delicious crunch!</b>

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:05.560
<b>Hot hot hot</b>

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:04.200
What is this?

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:07.790
Fried squid balls and fried squid rings.

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:11.830
<b>Hot hot hot</b>

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.530
<b>Squid Rings</b>

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.530
<b>Excellent with whatsontap</b>

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:11.830
A fried-food lover like 
you is sure to love it!

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:13.620
That's clever.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:17.070
This way neither the look nor the 
smell will betray that it's squid.

00:04:17.350 --> 00:04:19.210
And it goes just great with some whatsontap.

00:04:20.330 --> 00:04:24.580
I'm sure the hot fried food goes 
perfectly with the cold whatsontap.

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.550
There's no way this won't be a good match!

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:27.920
Finally!

00:04:27.920 --> 00:04:29.360
Berthold-san!

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:32.190
I'm sorry, Taishou!

00:04:32.190 --> 00:04:33.580
He squidn't go.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:38.630
I am ink-credibly sorry, but with my 
skills, there is nothing more I can do.

00:04:38.630 --> 00:04:41.260
<i>Even Taishou's given up.</i>

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:43.860
<i>Now the ends justify all means!</i>

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:46.550
If he won't go, let's make him go.

00:04:46.550 --> 00:04:47.890
We'll go on the offen-squid!

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.360
Operation: Northern Wind and Sunshine!

00:04:50.700 --> 00:04:52.390
Eva-chan, may I?

00:04:52.390 --> 00:04:53.340
Yes?

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.160
<b>Crunch</b>

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:00.710
<b>Crispy</b>

00:04:59.790 --> 00:05:04.020
It's so crispy and chewy, 
and absolutely delicious!

00:05:01.050 --> 00:05:02.750
<b>Chewy</b>

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:06.340
<i>It's working.</i>

00:05:06.340 --> 00:05:08.520
<i>Just wait and see.</i>

00:05:08.520 --> 00:05:10.240
Next up is a fried squid ball.

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.270
Aah, it's so sweet and fluffy!

00:05:14.270 --> 00:05:16.680
The squid balls are amazing, too!

00:05:16.980 --> 00:05:18.430
What do you say?

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:21.620
Look at that smile and tell 
me you don't want to try it.

00:05:21.980 --> 00:05:25.040
Eva-chan's smile is like the sun.

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:27.280
I want my own children soon.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.230
<i>Wrong topic.</i>

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:34.040
Um, maybe this is just my own idea,

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:39.050
but did you maybe have a bad 
experience with squid?

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.740
That's it.

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:47.690
My great-grandfather was a sailor 
on a large traveling merchant ship.

00:05:48.260 --> 00:05:51.900
A crew of strong men of 
the sea who knew no fear,

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:55.860
and still there was one thing 
that terrified them.

00:05:56.740 --> 00:05:58.830
A monster so terrible it 
could devour entire ships.

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:00.130
That's the squid!

00:06:01.780 --> 00:06:06.280
Nobody ever survived an encounter 
with that awful being.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.770
I-Is that true?

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:10.800
It is.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:12.930
My great-grandfather 
experienced it firsthand.

00:06:13.300 --> 00:06:14.420
Make no mistake.

00:06:14.420 --> 00:06:18.190
B-But won't you be fine as long 
as you stay out of the ocean?

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:19.340
No.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.820
This scar is from a squid.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:26.190
We were on a drizzling battlefield.

00:06:26.690 --> 00:06:31.490
That day, I happened to eat 
some squid without noticing.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:39.090
I had eaten but a bite,

00:06:39.090 --> 00:06:43.900
but still he sent a mercenary wearing 
a squid-shaped helmet after me!

00:06:45.040 --> 00:06:46.980
N-No way!

00:06:47.310 --> 00:06:49.730
This, from a mere bite of dried squid.

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.980
If I eat fresh squid dishes, 
I'll be cursed for sure!

00:06:53.980 --> 00:06:59.130
I'm so sorry, but I cannot overcome 
my fear of the giant squid!

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:03.000
My life is already cursed by the squid!

00:07:03.270 --> 00:07:05.870
Um...

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.650
Wh-What's wrong, Eva-chan?

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:12.770
I ate so much of that squid!

00:07:12.770 --> 00:07:16.520
I was just trying to help Berthold-san.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:19.400
Am I going to be squid-cursed now?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:21.660
Th-That's—

00:07:22.570 --> 00:07:26.200
Look, you made a little girl cry.

00:07:26.200 --> 00:07:27.880
That's not—

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.060
I mean...

00:07:32.230 --> 00:07:34.350
Look at poor Eva-chan.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:35.710
That's right!

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:38.910
How are you going to make 
this right, Berthold-san?

00:07:40.440 --> 00:07:42.070
I won't...

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:44.950
I won't...

00:07:46.790 --> 00:07:47.620
To squid?

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:48.440
Or not to squid?

00:07:48.440 --> 00:07:56.040
I won't let you suffer 
this fear by... yourself!

00:07:57.220 --> 00:07:58.620
<i>He squid it!</i>

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.100
The c-curse!

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:10.130
The curse of the giant squid tries 
to spread through my mouth!

00:08:10.130 --> 00:08:11.950
But it squidn't!

00:08:11.950 --> 00:08:14.630
This is too crispy and chewy and delicious!

00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:13.140
<b>Crispy crispy crispy crispy</b>

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:14.140
<b>Chewy chewy chewy chewy</b>

00:08:15.330 --> 00:08:16.280
So good.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:18.200
How are you so delicious, squid?

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.410
I never knew it was this good.

00:08:20.410 --> 00:08:21.440
Taishou.

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:23.420
Why not show him an unprepared squid?

00:08:23.710 --> 00:08:26.420
Berthold-san, this is a squid.

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:27.750
I know that.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:29.390
That's a baby squid.

00:08:29.390 --> 00:08:32.150
If they were always that 
big, I'd have no problem.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:34.420
But they get bigger and bigger!

00:08:34.760 --> 00:08:36.420
This is an adult squid.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:38.460
Wh-What...

00:08:38.770 --> 00:08:40.900
You mean they don't get huge?

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:41.840
Nope.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:45.020
Sounds like your great-grandfather 
told you some tall tales.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:50.360
I mean, how could it be a firsthand 
experience if everyone there died?

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:53.580
Well, that's good, isn't it, Berthold-san?

00:08:54.570 --> 00:08:57.960
I've been had for a patsy, all this time.

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:01.470
What to do with this squid-induced rage?!

00:09:01.470 --> 00:09:02.550
Taishou!

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:04.880
Give me all the squid cuisine you got!

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:06.870
I've got a lot of wasted 
time to make up for.

00:09:07.340 --> 00:09:08.140
Coming right up.

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:11.140
You have some nerve, 
tormenting me this long.

00:09:12.200 --> 00:09:13.100
<b>Slurp</b>

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.500
<b>Smooth</b>

00:09:14.770 --> 00:09:18.500
Sweet and supple, this squid 
soumen is just great!

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:25.130
The texture is different 
once it gets cooked.

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:25.140
<b>Springy springy</b>

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:28.460
These crispy, chewy squid 
rings are good, too.

00:09:26.680 --> 00:09:28.980
<b>Crispy crispy</b>

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:33.140
Squid balls! Perfectly fried so the fluffy 
inside falls apart inside your mouth,

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.950
<b>Fluffy fluffy</b>

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:35.490
lifting up your heart.

00:09:35.490 --> 00:09:37.340
And then, pickled squid.

00:09:37.340 --> 00:09:42.180
I love the way the rich umami oozes 
out of it and this lively texture!

00:09:38.890 --> 00:09:42.630
<b>Ooze</b>

00:09:42.490 --> 00:09:43.810
Grilled squid tentacles!

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:47.900
Who would've thought that a creepy 
creature's legs could be this tasty?

00:09:48.570 --> 00:09:49.900
Fizz

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.320
The whatsontap goes just 
perfect with it, too!

00:09:58.380 --> 00:10:00.570
<i>I've defeated the squid.</i>

00:10:00.940 --> 00:10:03.810
<i>I'm coming for you, Hermina!</i>

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:10.460
I've returned, Hermina!

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.890
<b>Northern beach of the Empire</b>

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:14.260
Welcome home, Father!

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:14.260
<b>Hermina (16)
Daughter of the Squid Fisherman</b>

00:10:14.900 --> 00:10:17.250
Take a look at this huge thing!

00:10:17.250 --> 00:10:20.030
Wow, that's an impressive kraken.

00:10:20.030 --> 00:10:23.170
I hope Berthold-san will love it, too.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:31.290
Next up, we have Nobu Plus.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:33.040
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:35.020
<b>Nobu</b>

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:38.920
The popular train station bento 
taste, easily recreated at home!

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:38.920
<b>Narrator 
Teiyu Ichiryusai</b>

00:10:39.650 --> 00:10:45.440
Ryuuta Kijima is going to put his own 
spin on the dishes featured in Nobu!

00:10:42.150 --> 00:10:45.920
<b>Ryuuta Kijima Creates Nobu Dishes</b>

00:10:45.920 --> 00:10:49.120
I know people who refuse to eat squid.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:49.630
Really?

00:10:49.120 --> 00:10:52.240
They say they don't like it in its original shape.

00:10:49.530 --> 00:10:55.730
<b>Ryuuta Kijima
Grew up in a household where his grandmother and his mother 
were culinary researchers, so he got into cooking at an early age.
 Now he's a culinary researcher popular for his simple but serious 
recipes and fun presentation.</b>

00:10:52.240 --> 00:10:52.940
True, they do.

00:10:52.940 --> 00:10:55.420
Looks like this time, Berthold-san was the same.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:55.980
So, today's menu?

00:10:55.980 --> 00:10:58.070
Today, we're making ika meshi (squid rice).

00:10:58.070 --> 00:10:58.580
Like station bentos?

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:03.140
It's a squid dish, it's a rice dish, 
but it great while drinking.

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:03.880
Sounds good.

00:11:03.140 --> 00:11:06.350
And I think the ika meshi I have planned 
for today pairs just perfectly with sake.

00:11:03.370 --> 00:11:06.340
<b>Easy squid rice that 
pairs perfectly with sake</b>

00:11:06.380 --> 00:11:11.350
<b>Ika Meshi Style Sticky Rice, 
using dried cuttlefish and mochi 
[Ingredients (serves 2)]
 10g dried squid 
1 piece mochi
 1 cup rice
 3 green onions 
 3 slices ginger (thinly cut)
 Water as needed 
1 Tbsp soy sauce 
1 Tbsp sugar</b>

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:09.880
Ika meshi style sticky rice, using 
dried cuttlefish and mochi.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:11.340
This is all we need?

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:14.610
Usually mochi rice is used to make
 ika meshi, but today, we'll use regular rice.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:14.910
Huh?

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:18.960
Our secret weapon is mochi. If you cook
 this together with the regular rice,

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:22.240
you'll get the same glutinous 
consistency of mochi rice.

00:11:22.240 --> 00:11:24.990
You don't see any fresh squid here, right?

00:11:24.990 --> 00:11:27.120
This is dried shredded squid.

00:11:27.120 --> 00:11:29.760
Cooking this together in there 
recreates that soft texture.

00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:30.260
Amazing!

00:11:30.260 --> 00:11:32.900
I'll wash the rice now. A little hint.

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:33.340
All ears.

00:11:33.340 --> 00:11:34.750
It'll push the flavor to the next level.

00:11:34.750 --> 00:11:35.470
Teach me!

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:38.730
Use plenty of water. Splash it! 
Then stir it well.

00:11:38.730 --> 00:11:40.080
Splash it? Okay.

00:11:40.080 --> 00:11:42.540
Now, we're going to thoroughly 
drain the water once.

00:11:42.540 --> 00:11:43.700
Add a little bit of water.

00:11:43.700 --> 00:11:47.120
If there's lots of water now, the grains 
of rice can't polish each other so well,

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.930
so use your fingertips to agitate the rice.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.070
That concludes the washing.

00:11:52.070 --> 00:11:52.570
That's it?!

00:11:52.570 --> 00:11:56.000
When you're done with that, put it 
into a strainer and let it sit.

00:11:56.330 --> 00:11:57.520
Let's cut the ingredients now.

00:11:57.520 --> 00:12:02.720
First the mochi. When you buy the 
packaged mochi, it has grooves.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.260
I think cutting along those 
grooves is the easiest.

00:12:05.260 --> 00:12:07.990
Is this the secret to the glutinous effect?

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:08.860
Now the squid.

00:12:08.860 --> 00:12:10.920
Presenting the star of 
the show, the dried squid!

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:14.380
Please cut them so that the pieces are 
easy to eat when they're in the rice.

00:12:14.380 --> 00:12:14.750
Roger!

00:12:14.750 --> 00:12:18.220
Edwin-san was eating shutou 
in that bonito episode.

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.680
In the squid episode, he was 
eating squid shiokara.

00:12:20.680 --> 00:12:22.350
He seems to enjoy those 
types of snacks, huh?

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:22.950
We'd get along.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:26.070
The ginger, I like to slice it thinly.

00:12:26.070 --> 00:12:28.030
You really are good with that.

00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:30.920
Let's put the ingredients 
in the rice cooker.

00:12:30.920 --> 00:12:33.570
First the rice, of which 
we have one cup today.

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:37.460
Soy sauce, sugar.

00:12:38.640 --> 00:12:41.340
When making rice like this, add 
the water before the ingredients.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.620
If the other ingredients are in, you 
can't add the exact amount anymore.

00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:47.150
<b>Add the water before the other ingredients!</b>

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.170
And now the other ingredients.

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.920
<b>Adding the ingredients</b>

00:12:47.150 --> 00:12:50.920
<b>Add dried squid (10g), thinly sliced ginger, 1 piece of mochi</b>

00:12:47.170 --> 00:12:50.940
Add the dried squid, ginger,
 and mochi, then go!

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:51.930
How's it look?!

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:55.350
<b>40 minutes later</b>

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:54.210
It's done now. Let's take a look!

00:12:55.360 --> 00:12:58.590
Mix it well and thoroughly envelop 
the rice with the mochi.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:00.100
That will give it that 
nice glutinous texture.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:00.620
Let's see that.

00:13:00.620 --> 00:13:03.690
Mix it with a slicing motion.

00:13:05.100 --> 00:13:07.830
It really turned into glutinous rice!

00:13:07.830 --> 00:13:09.300
Now it's done.

00:13:09.300 --> 00:13:13.860
I've used dried squid for this, and the drying
 process really concentrates the flavor.

00:13:09.670 --> 00:13:18.010
<b>Ika meshi style sticky rice, 
using dried cuttlefish and mochi</b>

00:13:13.860 --> 00:13:18.000
The umami from the squid spreads throughout 
the rice, and I think it's really good.

00:13:18.010 --> 00:13:21.690
The trick of cooking rice with mochi 
opens up all sorts of possibilities,

00:13:21.690 --> 00:13:23.780
so please, try it at home.

00:13:23.780 --> 00:13:26.600
The dried squid and mochi are 
doing work in this recipe!

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:29.530
Yes, this really does taste 
like the station bento!

00:13:29.530 --> 00:13:32.760
It's really easy, so everyone, 
please try this at home!

